{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {}, "duration_s": 26.1, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "validate bimodal pattern robustness or fresh observation per D083", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": false, "summary": "E209 IT code entrant measurement completed successfully. Prototype tools/it_code_entrant_v2.py and tools/it_entrant_advisor.py measure segment newcomer fractions for 5 USAspending PSC codes using FY2023 current vs FY2018-2022 prior window comparison via the API's meta.total for complete census. Key finding: bimodal entry pattern unlike NIH SBIR's unimodal common-entry pattern. Federal IT shows 2 codes with significant sub-threshold entry (DA01: 0.2677, 7A21: 0.2912), 1 surviving the 0.30 kill gate (DA10: 0.3113), and 2 with 0 newcomers (7030, D304). This closes the 'fragmented ⇒ entry' inference transfer from NIH SBIR to federal IT. Experiment result recorded at EXPERIMENTS/E209-it-code-entrant/RESULT.md. Artifacts declared: tools/it_code_entrant_v2.py, tools/it_entrant_advisor.py, EXPERIMENTS/E209-it-code-entrant/RESULT.md. Next action: validate bimodal pattern robustness across additional PSC codes, or pursue fresh observation in new domain per D083.", "unlogged_changes": 30}, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 35, "session": "2026-10-21-017-complete-e209-it-code-entrant-measuremen", "ts": "2026-10-21T12:19:44+00:00"}
